-- title:
--   Surjectivity of the first reduction map on places
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, an integer $N \ge 1$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$. Let `data` consist of a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ annihilating the $q$-th level modular $j$-pair, let `hKr` be the Kronecker congruence asserting that the reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $q$ equals $(C(X)^q - X)\,(C(X) - X^q)$ in $(\mathbb Z/q)[X][Y]$, and let `hα`, `hβ` assert that the two Hecke embeddings `heckeAlphaBar`, `heckeBetaBar` of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebras from the base-changed full modular function field of level $N$ into that of level $Nq$ inside Laurent series are integral ring homomorphisms. Given a place specialization $P$ for these data, the assertion is that the map
--   $$\mathrm{reduceFst}\colon W \mapsto P.\mathrm{sp}\bigl(W|_{\mathrm{heckeAlphaBar}}\bigr)$$
--   from places of the level-$Nq$ base-changed full modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ to places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$ over $k$ — the subfield of $k((q))$ generated by the mod-$q$ reductions of the $j$-expansion and of its level-$N$ twist — is surjective, where $W|_{\mathrm{heckeAlphaBar}}$ denotes restriction of the place $W$ along the first degeneracy embedding `heckeAlphaBar`.
--
--   This says that every place of the level-$N$ special fibre over $k$ is hit by a place of the level-$Nq$ curve in characteristic zero, so that points of the reduced curve — in particular those lying over supersingular crossings — may be lifted before being analysed. It feeds the prolongation-tuple lemmas that extract nodal coordinates and inertia-stable data from a place specialization.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_PlaceSpecialization_reduceFst_surjective.lean

